  "description": "Our Strasbourg is an ode to an unforgettable stage victory in the 1971 Tour de France in which Eddy Merckx confirmed his class during a sprint against Roger De Vlaeminck on a dirt track. The St is the steel version of the Strasbourg. Steel is more budget-friendly than carbon. It is durable, stiff and yet comfortable. Compared to aluminium, steel has more elasticity, resulting in more comfort. The cabling is not integrated, making maintenance easier. Thanks to its gravel geometry, the Strasbourg offers comfort, stability and control even on the most barbaric roads. The Strasbourg St is perfect for the gravel rider looking for a versatile and comfortable bike.",
